248
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:27,420
You've had 50 years of your
lickety lifespan drained by Mama.

249
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:30,220
So that now puts you at 77. Seven.

250
00:18:31,780 --> 00:18:32,610
Interesting.

251
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:35,133
I wonder how many years you've got left.

252
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:37,340
Doesn't matter.

253
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:39,542
I'll choose where to die myself.

254
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:41,930
Hm.

255
00:18:42,013 --> 00:18:42,980
Enough about that.

256
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:46,342
You were captain of the
Nox pirates, weren't you?

257
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:49,360
Doesn't Nox mean night?

258
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:51,306
Ooh, that sounds rather dark.

259
00:18:51,480 --> 00:18:53,362
What's with the negativity, huh?

260
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:56,517
Every night comes to an end, as they say.

261
00:18:56,600 --> 00:18:58,780
In that case

262
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,300
Nox could mean Before the dawn

263
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:05,080
You Karoo understand

264
00:19:07,460 --> 00:19:10,457
The men who I admire Are
awaiting the dawn of the

265
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:14,020
new world All I want is to
lay its foundation For them

266
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:18,220
If I have enough time
for that I can die happy

267
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:24,340
You once said That before the dawn

268
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:27,746
And Nox were synonymous
with one another, yes?

269
00:19:28,420 --> 00:19:31,217
It's such a shame that the
only Nox you'll come to

270
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:34,660
know is the eternal darkness
that awaits in your death.

271
00:19:34,980 --> 00:19:35,940
Not quite.

272
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:47,310
Roger!

273
00:19:47,393 --> 00:19:48,223
Lord Odin!

274
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:49,620
Let me go, too!

275
00:19:50,580 --> 00:19:51,960
I'll do anything!

276
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:53,680
Just give me a chance!

277
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:57,780
Sorry, kiddo.

278
00:19:58,080 --> 00:19:59,940
You're not quite ready yet.

279
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:02,180
I'm not a kid! I'm Pedro!

280
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:11,020
The truth is I don't have much time left.

281
00:20:12,540 --> 00:20:13,370
Don't worry.

282
00:20:13,453 --> 00:20:16,433
Everyone will have a day when
it's their moment to shine.

283
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:20,337
Wait and you'll see.

284
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:22,697
Trust me, you'll know
when your time has come.

285
00:20:22,780 --> 00:20:25,540
You just got to stick it out until then.

286
00:20:27,540 --> 00:20:29,920
It was nice meeting you, Pedro.

287
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:34,020
I get it. Thank you.

288
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:45,750
Pedro!

289
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:46,950
Huh?

290
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:47,950
It's Roger.

291
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:50,812
Whoa, what's with that look on your face?

292
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:59,737
Long ago, roger told me.

293
00:20:59,820 --> 00:21:02,517
Everyone will get a chance to shine!

294
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:04,920
What are you rambling about?

295
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:06,720
It's finally my turn.

296
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:13,522
This should be more than enough
to undo all of your little tricks!

297
00:21:13,860 --> 00:21:15,060
That's dynamite!

298
00:21:15,220 --> 00:21:16,279
You wouldn't dare!

299
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:18,031
Have you lickety lost it?

300
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:30,940
I'm sorry, but I had a feeling
that this would be my final voyage.

301
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,920
What do you mean, Pedro?

302
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:40,320
Don't do it!

303
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:42,870
Adios.

304
00:22:11,820 --> 00:22:13,980
What do you mean, Pedro?

305
00:22:14,460 --> 00:22:17,880
One day, Yugara will
understand my decision.

306
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:23,840
No, it was to keep Luffy and his crew
alive so they can continue onward.

307
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:28,920
Pedro, no!

308
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:36,900
Listen, Yugaro must keep
moving forward! Pedro!

309
00:22:39,220 --> 00:22:40,680
No, Press.

310
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:42,530
What?

311
00:22:45,940 --> 00:22:49,000
Oh, I hope Mama and
Minister Perospero are okay.

312
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:51,380
It looks like they got blown up.

313
00:23:04,140 --> 00:23:06,100
Their candy is melting down.

314
00:23:06,660 --> 00:23:07,680
Is Press dead?

315
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:14,380
Did Pedro give up his life for us?

316
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:17,884
Was this truly the only
option that we had left?

317
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:33,737
I thought that was going to
be the end for me for sure.

318
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:35,140
Are you two all right?

319
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:45,340
No, Karen, it's too late. Let me go.

320
00:23:45,580 --> 00:23:47,600
I need to help Pedro, don't he?

321
00:23:47,700 --> 00:23:50,220
He might be alive out there. You can't.

322
00:23:50,340 --> 00:23:51,360
You saw it too.

323
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:53,900
Pedro sacrificed himself for us.

324
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:57,729
He saved our lives because there
was no other way to escape.

325
00:23:58,020 --> 00:23:59,844
Don't let his death be in vain.

326
00:24:00,100 --> 00:24:00,930
Please, Karen.

327
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:06,420
Try the fly. Ready?

328
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:09,300
Yes, we're all set.

329
00:24:10,120 --> 00:24:11,157
Hey, Chopper, Rock.

330
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:13,122
You guys still with us up there?

331
00:24:15,760 --> 00:24:16,590
Huh?

332
00:24:16,673 --> 00:24:17,503
Jinbei? Yes!

333
00:24:17,586 --> 00:24:19,536
They're beginning to come around now!

334
00:24:20,140 --> 00:24:22,380
Alright then, it's time to set sail!

335
00:24:29,340 --> 00:24:31,693
Pedro bought us this time with his life!

336
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:34,115
No way I'm gonna let that go to waste!

337
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:37,840
We're getting out of here,
no matter what it takes!

338
00:24:43,500 --> 00:24:45,040
I'm serious.

339
00:24:47,620 --> 00:24:49,277
What's this about?

340
00:24:49,360 --> 00:24:52,360
You're all so emotional!

341
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:56,877
Go away.

342
00:24:56,960 --> 00:24:58,497
There's a second of death.

343
00:24:58,580 --> 00:24:59,840
Careful, Carrot.

344
00:25:12,220 --> 00:25:13,050
AHHHHHHH!

345
00:25:20,240 --> 00:25:22,377
Straighten up, get on your feet, Carrot.

346
00:25:22,460 --> 00:25:24,225
And take the blade once again.

347
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:27,120
She has no aptitude for swords.

348
00:25:28,040 --> 00:25:28,870
Pedro!

349
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:30,377
It's none of your business!

350
00:25:30,460 --> 00:25:33,872
Carrot will become a peerless
swordsman under my guidance!

351
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:36,977
There's more than one way to get stronger.

352
00:25:37,060 --> 00:25:40,472
Surely there's another route
that's better suited for her.

353
00:25:42,620 --> 00:25:43,717
What is this?

354
00:25:43,800 --> 00:25:47,357
Take a fighting stance.

355
00:25:47,440 --> 00:25:52,680
I have a feeling this may be
a better fit for you, Karoo!

356
00:25:58,700 --> 00:26:00,537
It's better to play to your advantages.

357
00:26:00,620 --> 00:26:03,477
I think you're quite
adept at aerial maneuvers,

358
00:26:03,560 --> 00:26:08,089
so Combine that with your electro and
you, Karoo, will be off to a good start!

359
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:09,030
Seriously?

360
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:11,150
Uh-huh.

361
00:26:11,233 --> 00:26:12,063
Try to attack me.

362
00:26:12,146 --> 00:26:14,780
I'll be your sparring partner. Okie Dock!

363
00:26:28,260 --> 00:26:32,337
I was starting to think I'd never
be strong like everyone else.

364
00:26:32,420 --> 00:26:35,517
I can't believe the
answer was here all along.

365
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:37,740
Thanks for teaching me this!

366
00:26:38,660 --> 00:26:40,897
It doesn't matter how you Karoo battle.

367
00:26:40,980 --> 00:26:44,360
Just keep honing your skills
and be ready for anything.

368
00:26:47,260 --> 00:26:49,197
I know you Karoo can do it.

369
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:50,120
Don't worry.

370
00:26:53,820 --> 00:26:54,940
I know it?

371
00:27:13,740 --> 00:27:17,580
You won't leave this
island as long as I'm here.

372
00:27:26,400 --> 00:27:28,880
Get off of her! Right now!

373
00:27:35,600 --> 00:27:37,520
Carrot, leave him to me!

374
00:27:45,340 --> 00:27:48,160
You think you're strong
enough to kick me off?

375
00:27:53,660 --> 00:27:54,840
We're leaving!

376
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:57,160
I'm the captain of this ship!

377
00:27:58,360 --> 00:27:59,357
Now, Gum-Gum!

378
00:27:59,440 --> 00:28:00,920
Elephant, don't go!

379
00:28:13,180 --> 00:28:17,497
Sales look good towards the northwest.

380
00:28:17,580 --> 00:28:21,320
Kaido burst azimuth 45
degrees to northwest!

381
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:26,597
Yes, going back will prevent
me from hurting your friends,

382
00:28:26,680 --> 00:28:28,957
even if you can see what's coming?

383
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:30,864
You can't stop us from leaving!

384
00:28:32,140 --> 00:28:34,260
Hey, brother, I'm here to save you!

385
00:28:34,780 --> 00:28:35,980
No, not now.

386
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:38,460
I won't let them escape.

387
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:42,527
All units, prepare to
fire on the enemy ship.

388
00:28:43,340 --> 00:28:44,340
Adjust elevation.

389
00:28:45,500 --> 00:28:46,330
Mr.

390
00:28:46,413 --> 00:28:47,820
Shark, it's time to boogie!

391
00:28:49,280 --> 00:28:50,300
Help me, Chopper.

392
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:51,537
Grab ahold of the rope.

393
00:28:51,620 --> 00:28:53,557
Let's pull our submersible
closer to the Sunny

394
00:28:53,640 --> 00:28:55,537
before they start
attacking the poor thing.

395
00:28:55,620 --> 00:28:56,450
Whoa, Carrot!

396
00:28:56,540 --> 00:28:57,557
Think you can stand up?

397
00:28:57,640 --> 00:28:58,477
Here, let me help you.

398
00:28:58,560 --> 00:28:59,390
I'm all right.

399
00:28:59,780 --> 00:29:01,560
Thank you, Tia Nami.

400
00:29:06,520 --> 00:29:07,777
Where is it?

401
00:29:07,860 --> 00:29:08,940
She caught up!

402
00:29:09,140 --> 00:29:10,493
This is gonna be messy.

403
00:29:10,760 --> 00:29:14,936
We have to get out of here quick
before she damages this Sunny anymore!

404
00:29:20,780 --> 00:29:21,880
It can't be!

405
00:29:22,160 --> 00:29:23,180
Is that Pedro?

406
00:29:23,480 --> 00:29:24,700
So he did survive!

407
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:41,300
He almost had me.

408
00:29:41,700 --> 00:29:43,080
That isn't Pedro!

409
00:29:43,360 --> 00:29:44,320
It's Candy Guy!

410
00:29:44,660 --> 00:29:47,340
He was actually fighting
for a second there.

411
00:29:47,700 --> 00:29:51,180
That crazy mink lickety
left with my candy armor.

412
00:29:53,740 --> 00:29:54,900
That's unfair!

413
00:29:55,240 --> 00:29:56,617
Why is he alive?

414
00:29:56,700 --> 00:29:58,040
And not Pedro!

415
00:30:00,700 --> 00:30:03,677
It appears all our cannonballs
were intercepted this time!

416
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:04,590
Third round.

417
00:30:04,680 --> 00:30:06,621
Hurry up and prepare the cannons.

418
00:30:08,500 --> 00:30:09,920
Let go!

419
00:30:10,960 --> 00:30:12,520
Carrot! Inami!

420
00:30:13,100 --> 00:30:13,980
Jinbei!

421
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:16,310
Brook!

422
00:30:16,393 --> 00:30:17,223
Chopper!

423
00:30:34,660 --> 00:30:35,620
Listen up!

424
00:30:36,280 --> 00:30:37,540
I'll be right back!

425
00:30:37,860 --> 00:30:39,448
Can you hold down the fort?

426
00:30:39,980 --> 00:30:42,340
Murphy, what are you two talking about?

427
00:30:45,200 --> 00:30:49,906
When the lever returns to its original
position, the refill process is complete.

428
00:30:50,260 --> 00:30:51,201
Okay, everybody.

429
00:30:51,380 --> 00:30:52,797
Better hold on to something.

430
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:54,180
Death grip commenced.

431
00:30:54,300 --> 00:30:56,617
Too ready for takeoff
when you are, Jinbei.

432
00:30:56,700 --> 00:30:58,229
We're good over here, too!

433
00:30:59,680 --> 00:31:01,500
Right! Let's go!

434
00:31:02,780 --> 00:31:05,820
Don't let the target get away. Now fire!

435
00:31:09,340 --> 00:31:10,170
It's time!

436
00:31:10,520 --> 00:31:13,160
Lastly, don't forget to shout!

437
00:31:13,800 --> 00:31:15,080
We're running!

438
00:31:19,100 --> 00:31:21,277
Kaku now burst!

439
00:31:21,360 --> 00:31:23,040
Burst!

440
00:31:24,360 --> 00:31:25,380
Burst!

441
00:31:25,860 --> 00:31:26,860
Super!

442
00:31:42,980 --> 00:31:44,840
Amand reporting in.

443
00:31:45,240 --> 00:31:48,900
The enemy has escaped by air. It's what?

444
00:31:53,460 --> 00:31:55,140
Hey, where's Loopy?

445
00:31:59,940 --> 00:32:01,560
Is that Straw Hat?

446
00:32:01,720 --> 00:32:03,014
What, get out of here!

447
00:32:15,260 --> 00:32:16,440
Well played.

448
00:32:17,420 --> 00:32:20,160
Now I can fight you
without any interruptions.

449
00:32:22,880 --> 00:32:23,780
No way!

450
00:32:23,980 --> 00:32:25,333
That was his path back!

451
00:32:25,440 --> 00:32:27,499
What the hell is that guy thinking?

452
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:41,920
So that's your captain's
determination, Val.

453
00:32:43,860 --> 00:32:45,640
But you're no match for me.

454
00:32:46,040 --> 00:32:48,100
This place will be your grave.

455
00:32:49,780 --> 00:32:54,640
No, I'll go back to the sunny,
right after I kick your ass!
